## Microsoft Graph API Permissions

Reading requires `NetworkAccess.Read.All`; writing requires `NetworkAccess.ReadWrite.All`. Microsoft Graph documents both application and delegated permissions. Delegated callers also require an appropriate administrator role such as Global Secure Access Administrator or Security Administrator.

## Behavior Notes

- The policy and each rule have separate Terraform lifecycles. Set `tls_inspection_policy_id` to the parent resource ID.
- `enabled` is required and maps to the rule's API status; `status` reports that raw value. Unknown API statuses produce a diagnostic rather than being interpreted as disabled.
- Updates to name, description, action, priority, enabled and destinations preserve the rule ID. Changing the parent policy replaces the rule.
- Priorities must be unique per policy. The recommended bypass rule initially occupies priority 65000. For priority swaps, move one rule to an unused priority in a separate apply first.
- The system rule at priority 50 is outside this resource's supported scope. The recommended bypass rule can be imported explicitly using its parent and rule IDs.
- At least one destination group and one nonempty value per group are required by the provider. Group order is preserved; values are an unordered set.
- Omitting `description` clears it to null; an explicit empty string remains an empty string.

All CRUD operations default to a timeout of **3 minutes**. Configure `timeouts` to override them.

